      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current implementation for setting `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` uses a UID-based path, which will break parallel test execution.\n\nBecause the path is tied to `os.getuid()`, any concurrent test runs executed by the same user (e.g., testing multiple boards simultaneously locally or in a CI environment) will evaluate to the exact same directory (e.g., `/tmp/renode-config-1000`). When multiple Renode instances try to share the same configuration directory at the same time, it will lead to file lock errors, race conditions, and flaky tests.\n\n**Recommendation:**\nReplace the static path with `tempfile.mkdtemp()` to generate a unique directory for every run. This guarantees complete process isolation so parallel tests can run safely.\n\n```python\nimport tempfile\n\nos.environ.setdefault(\n    \"XDG_CONFIG_HOME\",\n    tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix\u003d\"renode-config-\")\n)\n\n```\n\n**Note on cleanup:** Because `os.execvp()` replaces the Python process, Python cannot automatically delete this directory when the test finishes. As a result, a new folder will be left in `/tmp` for every run. However, relying on the operating system\u0027s routine `/tmp` garbage collection is the standard and necessary trade-off here to enable safe concurrent testing.",
